# Stands in for the build directory every repository ignores.
#
# `generated/` is empty in a fresh checkout, and deliberately so: nothing
# ignored is committed here, because a file that is both tracked and ignored
# breaks `git add` — and so every pre-commit hook — for everyone who touches it
# afterwards. Populate it from the committed samples beside the corpus to watch
# discovery skip it:
#
#     cp -R projects/ic-suite/codometer/codometer-examples/examples/compiled projects/ic-suite/codometer/codometer-examples/examples/corpus/generated
#     codometer --directory examples/corpus --json | jq '.targets[0].files'   # still 28
#
# Codometer reads this file itself rather than invoking git, so the codebase
# target never sees `generated/` however many files are put in it — while a
# declared target's globs reach them anyway, which is the whole reason targets
# exist. See the package README's "Targets" section.
generated/
